      'Why the Formula Worked',
      'Many people describe Karikku as a simple comedy channel. That description misses what actually made it successful. Comedy was never the final product; relatability was.',
      'The scripts reflected situations that almost every Malayali had experienced: friendships, family dynamics, office politics, awkward conversations, financial struggles, and the humour hidden inside ordinary life. The audience laughed because they recognized their own lives. Actors like Anu K Aniyan became central to that experience because they never overshadowed the stories. Instead, they allowed the writing to breathe through performances that felt entirely effortless.',
      'In many ways, Karikku demonstrated that authenticity could become a massive competitive advantage in modern entertainment.',
      'Consistency Over Virality',
      'One viral video can introduce a creator. It cannot sustain a career. Long-term success requires consistency.',
