      'Modern audiences rarely separate creators from their work. The individual becomes the brand. For many traditional celebrities, this creates immense pressure to maintain a carefully constructed public image.',
      'Anu K Aniyan has largely avoided that trap. His public presence mirrors the exact qualities audiences associate with his performances: grounded, approachable, and uncomplicated. That consistency strengthens his personal brand because audiences experience the exact same personality whether they encounter him through media interviews, social updates, or scripted performances.',
      'Authenticity has become one of the strongest currencies in the creator economy. Anu built his career around it long before it became fashionable.',
      'The Business of Trust',
      'The entertainment industry often measures success through opening-day collections, follower counts, or fleeting viral moments. Yet the most valuable asset may be something less visible: trust.',
      'Trust determines whether audiences return for the next project. Trust determines whether brands want long-term partnerships. Trust determines whether filmmakers believe an actor can emotionally carry a story.',
